---
version: 2.0.2
title: sbom help
file: ./test/licence_audit/output_snapshot_test.gleam
test_name: sbom_help_test
---
Generate a CycloneDX 1.6 or SPDX 2.3 JSON SBOM from manifest.toml. Does not
evaluate licence policy. Includes all dependencies; CycloneDX records their
scope. JSON output stays plain in every color mode.

Command: sbom

USAGE:
    licence_audit sbom [ --cache-dir=<DIR> --color=<auto|always|never>
        --format=<cyclonedx-json|spdx-json> --licence-text --manifest=<PATH>
        --no-cache --offline --output=<PATH> --quiet --reproducible --verbose
        --vulns ]

FLAGS:
    --cache-dir=<DIR>                    Use DIR as the application cache root
                                         for all cache families

    --color=<auto|always|never>          Colorize output: auto|always|never
                                         (default auto; alias: --colour)

    --format=<cyclonedx-json|spdx-json>  Output format: cyclonedx-json or
                                         spdx-json

    --help                               Print help information

    --licence-text                       Embed canonical SPDX text (alias:
                                         --license-text); CycloneDX only,
                                         offline requires usable pinned text in
                                         the cache

    --manifest=<PATH>                    Read manifest from PATH

    --no-cache                           Bypass the on-disk caches

    --offline                            Prohibit network access; use local
                                         files and usable cached evidence.
                                         Required metadata, publication
                                         verification, and requested SPDX text
                                         must remain available

    --output=<PATH>                      Write SBOM to PATH instead of stdout
                                         (alias: -o)

    --quiet                              Suppress progress output (alias: -q)

    --reproducible                       Reproducible output from locked
                                         metadata, current local metadata, and
                                         publication evidence; serialNumber is a
                                         content hash and timestamp comes from
                                         SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH (default
                                         1970-01-01T00:00:00Z)

    --verbose                            Show detailed progress output (alias:
                                         -v)

    --vulns                              Query OSV.dev and embed a CycloneDX
                                         vulnerabilities array (requires
                                         network; conflicts with --offline and
                                         --reproducible)

